## Comparing Preparation Pathways

| Pathway / Activity | Core Focus | Key Strengths Developed | Limitations |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **LeetCode & Problem Solving** | Algorithmic efficiency, data structures, runtime optimization. | Passing automated coding screens, mastering Big-O analysis, spotting edge cases. | Lacks real-world architecture, team collaboration, and practical tooling practice. |
| **Hackathons** | Rapid MVP development, product pitching, API integration. | Hands-on experience with modern tech stacks, teamwork under deadlines, public presentation. | Code is often unrefined or unmaintainable due to extreme time constraints. |
| **Open Source Contribution** | Reading existing codebases, adhering to style guides, peer review. | Learning how production systems evolve, writing documentation, navigating large repos. | High initial learning curve; slow feedback cycles compared to competitive coding. |
| **Personal Projects** | Full-lifecycle software development from idea to deployment. | Architectural planning, devops/hosting experience, deep domain-specific knowledge. | Requires high self-discipline; lacks the immediate external feedback of coding judges or tests. |

